WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.170
Let's go next to our caller from the three
zero one area code.

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:09.209
There is something a little funky going on
with the call system today, but we're going

00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:13.379
to do our best to sort of work within what
is available to us.

00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:15.749
So who's calling from three Oh one today.

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:18.650
Hey David, this is Jason.

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:20.970
I'm from Hagerstown, Maryland.

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:23.710
Hey Jason, what's going on?

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:32.850
Oh yeah, my question is about fake news and
what we can do to combat it and if the government

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:35.850
should, um, have any role in that.

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:45.350
Um, so, um, I'm becoming increasingly concerned
about, um, fake news and these conspiracy

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:46.350
movements.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:54.170
Um, so just like anti vacs movements and um,
you know, like Fox news is defending Trump

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:58.050
at all costs and they're not grounded in reality.

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:04.790
Um, and things like climate change, they just
deny it when all scientists pretty much say

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:05.930
it's real.

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:12.080
Um, so I'm wondering what you think, um, we
can do to combat it and if the government

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:14.570
should have any, have any role in combat.

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:15.570
Okay.

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:19.950
So the, the, the problem is that when you
get to the point of arguing about or thinking

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:23.980
about whether the government should have any
role, it's sort of already too late.

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:28.890
Like if, if we have a society where we need
the government to combat fake news, we've

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:32.420
already sort of lost, and this goes back to
what I've been talking about, I talked about

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:33.810
it earlier this week.

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:40.210
We have an almost total lack of uh, schools
teaching people to really think for themselves

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:43.930
to understand epistemology, to understand
critical thinking.

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:50.270
And if an, until we have that, the government
combating fake news by putting restrictions

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:55.010
on Facebook or whatever the case may be, it's
too late in the process.

00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:57.440
We need to be attacking this far, far earlier.

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:02.410
Now, if someone has a particular proposal
as to something that could be done by law

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:08.030
to try to quote, fight fake news, I'm not
opposed to it reflexively like on principle,

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:09.720
I'm open to listening to it.

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:15.819
But the problem is that if we had more adults
who just understand media literacy, understand

00:02:15.819 --> 00:02:19.849
epistemology, understand arguments, understand
how to determine for themselves whether a

00:02:19.849 --> 00:02:24.209
conclusion that is being sped to us actually
follows from the premises.

00:02:24.209 --> 00:02:28.269
And whether the premises are precise and accurate,
we wouldn't be having the conversation about

00:02:28.269 --> 00:02:30.280
this government need to need to deal with
this.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:31.599
That's not the reality.

00:02:31.599 --> 00:02:36.170
Government is in the picture because things
have gotten so bad, but it needs to really

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:40.890
be dealt with systemically starting far earlier
than when we would just say government needs

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:42.849
to fix it.

00:02:42.849 --> 00:02:43.849
[inaudible]

00:02:43.849 --> 00:02:44.849
right.

00:02:44.849 --> 00:02:47.490
Yeah, I agree with that.

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:50.220
Um, I almost think it's too late at this point.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:53.920
Uh, I mean there's just like so many people
that are just like a little college.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:54.920
Yeah.

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:58.120
I mean it's never too late to start educating
people, but at this point a lot of people

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:04.709
lack the skills to really figure it out a
for for themselves, unfortunately.

00:03:04.709 --> 00:03:06.200
[inaudible]

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.680
exactly.

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:11.709
All right, well thank you.

